# "Whenever you commit a crime, put a +1/+1 counter on Lazav. Then you may exile a card from a graveyard. If a creature card was exiled this way, you may have Lazav become a copy of that card until end of turn. This ability triggers only once each turn." Turn 3: a Bolt at Bot2's Memnite is a crime: Lazav gets a counter and, with no card in a graveyard, nothing is asked; a second crime that turn (a Bolt at Bot2) triggers nothing more. Turn 5: a third Bolt at Bot2 is a crime; the graveyards hold two Bolts and the opponent's Memnite, Bot1 exiles the Memnite (a creature card) and Lazav becomes a copy of it until end of turn, keeping both counters; on turn 7 it is Lazav again, still with both.

